index 0000000..dc4c0f1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/entry-point.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+Feature: Application entry point
+  As a user opening the todo app in a browser
+  I want an index.html at the project root that loads the app
+  So that the todo app renders and runs
+
+  Rule: Entry point exists and is valid
+
+    Scenario: The project root contains an index.html
+      Given a file exists at "index.html"
+      Then the file "index.html" contains the text "<!doctype html>"
+
+    Scenario: index.html loads the application script
+      Given a file exists at "index.html"
+      Then the file "index.html" contains the text "<script src=\"js/app.js\">"
+
+    Scenario: index.html contains the todo input element
+      Given a file exists at "index.html"
+      Then the file "index.html" contains the text "new-todo"
+
+    Scenario: index.html contains the main section
+      Given a file exists at "index.html"
+      Then the file "index.html" contains the text "class=\"main\""
+
+    Scenario: index.html contains the footer section
+      Given a file exists at "index.html"
+      Then the file "index.html" contains the text "class=\"footer\""
